course: dictionary
lesson: 14709
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning is right. «Proceeds» is one of these words. Look at the clues in the sentence to decide what it means.
explain: As a noun, «the proceeds» means the money you get from selling something or from an event. «The bake sale raised £40, and all the proceeds went to the animal shelter.» The clues are bake sale and raised: the proceeds are the money taken in.
explain: As a verb, proceed means go on or move forward. «She proceeds to the next step.» Test your meaning by swapping in «goes on to». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: The proceeds are the money you get from selling something or from an event, such as a fair or a concert.
fact: «All proceeds go to charity» means every bit of the money raised is given away.
fact: As a verb, «proceeds» means goes on or moves forward: «She proceeds to eat her lunch.»
fact: In a formal sentence, «proceeds» can mean continues after a stop: «The lesson proceeds after the break.»
fact: The verb forms are proceed, proceeds, proceeded and proceeding.
exercise: The school fair made £120. «The proceeds went to the library fund.» What are the proceeds? | *The money taken in from the fair | The tables and chairs used | The list of who came | A prize for the best cake
exercise: «She proceeds to the next room.» What does proceeds mean here? | Stays still and waits | *Goes on or moves forward | Cleans the floor | Sells the room
exercise: «All proceeds go to charity.» What does this tell you? | *Every bit of the money raised is given away | Nobody gets any money at all | The charity is closed today | The charity sells its money
test: «The concert raised money, and the proceeds of the sale were counted.» What are the proceeds in this sentence? | The people who sang | *The money taken in from the sale | The tickets that were printed
test: «The lesson proceeds after the break.» What does proceeds mean? | Ends for the day | Goes backwards | Is cancelled | *Continues after a stop
exam: Which sentence uses proceeds as a verb meaning moves forward? | *After the bell, the class proceeds to the hall | The proceeds were counted by Sam | The proceeds of the cake sale were £30 | All the proceeds go to the zoo
